><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250522100859+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250522100912+10'00'" name="60d4a17b-acfe-4eb7-a743-d5820417ec36" page="5" coords="50.077100,408.542000,289.279000,408.542000,50.077100,398.746000,289.279000,398.746000,38.169700,398.109000,289.264000,398.109000,38.169700,388.313000,289.264000,388.313000,38.169700,387.620000,289.128000,387.620000,38.169700,377.825000,289.128000,377.825000,38.169700,377.187000,289.216000,377.187000,38.169700,367.392000,289.216000,367.392000,38.169700,366.698000,289.192000,366.698000,38.169700,356.903000,289.192000,356.903000,38.169700,356.265000,289.120000,356.265000,38.169700,346.470000,289.120000,346.470000,38.169700,345.776000,289.223000,345.776000,38.169700,335.981000,289.223000,335.981000,38.177600,335.343000,289.104000,335.343000,38.177600,325.548000,289.104000,325.548000,38.177600,324.855000,138.387000,324.855000,38.177600,315.059000,138.387000,315.059000" rect="37.863600,314.753000,289.585000,408.848000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Across a three-season period of professional level netball – most recorded&#xD;injuries were to the lower limb, particularly the knee and ankle.&#xD;Knee joint injuries, ankle tendon injuries, and knee synovitis/&#xD;patellofemoral pain were themost burdensome injuries; however, variation&#xD;in specific injury burden was observed between pre- and inseason&#xD;periods. Very few players avoided injury; and time-loss, nontime&#xD;loss and subsequent injuries were prominent – highlighting the&#xD;need for ongoing preventative and management strategies across all&#xD;players in elite-level netball.&#xD;&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>There remains a need for ongoing preventative efforts targeting lower&#xD;limb injuries in professional netball.&#xD;• The varying nature of professional netball injuries in pre- versus inseason&#xD;phases likely requires a different emphasis on preventative&#xD;and management efforts of support staff during these periods.&#xD;• The demand of non-time loss injuries on support staff time and&#xD;resources in managing players must be considered.&#xD;• These findings could be used to during the development of competition&#xD;fixtures and when determining the length of pre-season periods&#xD;to mitigate against injury risk.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="595.276000,316.542000,779.276000,408.542000"
/></highlight
